# Data model (app/prisma/schema.prisma)

Provider: MySQL. Prisma client generated at build and in CI. Field-level encryption via prisma-field-encryption annotations in comments.

Below is a relationship-oriented summary (not exhaustive fields).

- User
  - Fields: id, email (encrypted), emailHash (hash of email), password (encrypted), role, countryId, jwtKey, settings/config
  - Relations: budgets, accounts (UserAccount), plaidItems, notifications/dismissals, reconciliationPeriodsClosed
- Account
  - Fields: id (uuid), name, isDefault, isArchived
  - Relations: users (UserAccount), invites, reoccurrences, registers (AccountRegister), budgets, categories, snapshots, savingsGoals, bills, reconciliationPeriods
- UserAccount — membership and permissions per account, with allowedBudgetIds and allowedAccountRegisterIds JSON
- AccountInvite + AccountInviteAccount — invite and per-account permissions for invitee
- Budget — per Account; relations to registers, savingsGoals, notifications, bill profiles/instances, reconciliationPeriods
- AccountRegister — core ledger/register entity for an account and budget
  - Fields include: typeId (AccountType), name (encrypted), balances, creditLimit, PLAID linkage (plaidId, plaidAccessToken — encrypted + hash), asset/loan properties, minAccountBalance, vehicle details, walletAddress (encrypted + hash) for crypto, statement interval, various sort orders
  - Relations: entries (RegisterEntry), reoccurrences, splits target, bill profiles/instances, snapshots, savings goals (source/target), reconciliationPeriods, crypto chains and token balances, optional collateral
- RegisterEntry — transaction rows
  - Fields: description (encrypted), amount, balance, flags (projected, pending, cleared, matched, balance/manual), typeId, plaid linkage (encrypted + hash), categoryId, timestamps
  - Relations: register, reoccurrence, category, reconciliationItems, paid bill instances, reconciliation closing entry
- Category — hierarchical (parent/children via subCategoryId), scoped optionally to account
  - Used by entries, reoccurrences, splits, and as default payment/interest categories on registers
  - Note: a functional unique index for (account_id, IFNULL(sub_category_id,''), name) exists via migration
- Reoccurrence — scheduled transaction definition for a register
  - Fields: intervalId (+ count), amount, description (encrypted), categoryId, weekend adjustments, optional transferAccountRegisterId, amount adjustment strategy (mode/direction/value/interval)
  - Relations: entries (emitted from this), skips, splits, plaid name aliases, billProfile/instances
- ReoccurrenceSplit — splits a reoccurrence across transfer registers, with fixed/percent modes
- ReoccurrenceSkip — per-occurrence skip markers
- ReoccurrencePlaidNameAlias — normalized Plaid names mapped to a reoccurrence for matching
- SavingsGoal — sources and targets funds between two registers within a budget
- Bills
  - BillProfile (kind: BILL/INCOME/TRANSFER) — encapsulates a reoccurrence with metadata like payee, expected ranges, reminders, priority
  - BillInstance — concrete scheduled/paid instances with status, dueAt, paidAt, paidAmount, linkage to entry
- Reconciliation
  - ReconciliationPeriod — OPEN/CLOSED, with statement balances, dates, closing adjustment linkage, closedByUser
  - ReconciliationItem — links register entries to a period and clearance status
- Snapshots
  - AccountSnapshot — per Account at a time
  - AccountRegisterSnapshot — per register in a snapshot (name, balances, type)
  - RegisterEntrySnapshot — point-in-time entry data for the snapshot
  - AccountRegisterSummary — summary rows by month/year
- Notifications
  - NotificationEvent — active events (FORECAST_RISK, REOCCURRENCE_HEALTH), deduped by (userId,budgetId,kind,fingerprint|occurrenceKey)
  - NotificationDismissal — suppressions by occurrenceKey
- Integrations & logs
  - PlaidItem, PlaidSyncCursor, PlaidSyncLog (captures tx counts, errors, durations)
  - IntegrationAlert, IntegrationJobLog — generic alerting/job logs
  - OpenAiRequestLog — request/response metrics
- Types & config
  - AccountType — type, name, class, isCredit, accruesBalanceGrowth
  - Interval — interval catalog (shared across registers & reoccurrences)
  - Rsa — RSA key material (id, isDefault, keypair)
- Cash and Crypto
  - CashOnHand — per register denomination counts
  - EvmChain — chain catalog (networkId, symbol)
  - CryptoRegisterChain — allowed chains for a crypto register
  - CryptoTokenBalance — token holdings and USD valuation per register

Encrypted fields (selected):
- User.email, User.password
- AccountRegister.name, plaidId, plaidAccessToken, walletAddress (+ hash columns for deterministic lookups)
- RegisterEntry.description, plaidId (+ hash)
- Reoccurrence.description

Microservice model (microservice/prisma/schema.prisma): subset aligned to maintenance needs (accounts, users, registers, entries, reoccurrences, snapshots, types, RSA, Plaid cursor/items, etc.). It intentionally omits some app-only models (e.g., notifications, bills in older snapshot). Always consult both schemas before cross-package changes.
